        <dc:title>London Calling</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Ravenwood, Nathan &amp; Kadath" opf:role="aut">Ravenwood, Nathan</dc:creator>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Ravenwood, Nathan &amp; Kadath" opf:role="aut">Kadath</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (3.42.0) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2018-10-15T00:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;p&gt;Sebastian is a consummate bachelor, a game developer living in London who enjoys a casual relationship with his friends Diamond and Puzzle. One night, a co-worker drags him to a local punk bar, where he meets Tishala, a free-spirited hyena for whom age is nothing but a number. Initially the reason for him returning to the bar frequently, Seb also meets Dom, a hunky ram who sings for one of the bands that frequent the club. Both the hyena and the ram entrance him and scratch both sides of his desires, and Seb is quick to delve into debauchery with the both of them.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However, Tish and Dom have some kind of history, and operate with a clear disdain for one another. Seb is confident he can keep the two of them in his orbit without them finding out about his relationship with the other. After all, neither of them want a full-fledged relationship with him. But as the days go on and he's worn out by the non-stop sex with both his paramores, the secret becomes harder and harder to keep, and Seb begins to question just what it is he's actually doing.   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Can Seb find a happy medium with Tish and Dom that satisfies everyone? Or will he get burned in the end?   &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LONDON CALLING is a 40,000 word novella of casual bisexual encounters set against the backdrop of London's punk scene. It contains male/female and male/male adult scenes. Based on the Londoners comic series by Kadath.&lt;/p&gt;</dc:description>
